+## Following release: Rails 7.2 defaults
+
+`Gemfile.next` uses Rails 7.2.4 on the same Ruby, with 7.0 defaults for
+normal testing. Both bundles share local and plugin Gemfiles. The probe
+also boots the candidate on 7.2 defaults with the proposed rollback
+exceptions (`REDMINE_TEST_RAILS_72_DEFAULTS=1`, test environment only).
+Roll Rails 7.0 out everywhere before promoting 7.2; after 7.2 serves traffic,
+roll back to this Rails 7.0 release, not Rails 6.1.
+
+When promoting 7.2, make `config.load_defaults 7.2` unconditional and
+carry forward the tested exceptions:
+
+* Keep Marshal cookie payloads and disable the new message metadata writer
+  (`config.active_support.use_message_serializer_for_metadata = false`).
+  Rails 7.0 cannot read the new metadata envelope used for cookie purposes
+  and mail token purposes/expiry.
+* Keep `config.active_support.message_serializer = :marshal`. Rails 7.0
+  expects Marshal mail token payloads; the new JSON writer changes payload
+  types and is not readable by the rollback target. These are writer
+  restrictions, not relaxations of signature, purpose or expiry checks.
+* Keep per-form CSRF disabled during the rollback window. Keep the legacy
+  SHA-1 reader rotations as long as Rails 6.1 artifacts can still be valid.
+* Use cache format 7.0 on Rails 7.2: it cannot select 6.1 as a writer, and
+  Rails 7.0 can read 7.0 entries. Do not depend on Rails 7.2 reading old 6.1
+  entries. For shared stores, use a separate namespace for 7.2 caches if
+  necessary; do not flush unrelated keys or store login state in that cache.
+* Keep `ActiveRecord::Coders::YAMLColumn` as the default column serializer
+  until models and plugins explicitly declare their existing coders. This
+  preserves the database format when rolling back.
+
+Before promotion run the complete test suite under 7.2 defaults, rehearse
+with production adapters and plugins, and check shared caches and queued
+jobs (including jobs carrying serialized records). Do not combine the
+framework promotion with irreversible database or data-format changes.
+Narrow or remove the temporary overrides in a later release only after
+its rollback target can read the new artifacts and old artifacts have
+expired or been migrated.
+
